  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to improve the living conditions of 8,794 direct beneficiaries (6,970 refugees and 1,824 host people) in line in North Uganda The key result areas include: (i) strengthening the referral pathways and the quality care of MCH health services in Madi Okollo Terego districts (ii) improving   RMNCH service delivery in Madi Okollo and Terego districts through equipping, supplies and community engagement.</narrative>
